  "result": "The discount check was off by one, and it's fixed now.\n\n**Cause:** in `shop/pricing.py:10`, `line_subtotal` used `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD` with the threshold set to 10. Only 11 or more units got the 5% discount, so an order of exactly 10 got none.\n\n**Fix:** changed the comparison to `>=`, so 10 or more units now get the discount, matching the policy.\n\n**Tests:** all 7 pass. The existing `test_bulk_discount` checks exactly 10 units and expects 1028 cents, so it would have caught this bug. I didn't run it before the fix, but with the old check that order comes to 1083 cents, so the test would have failed. I also added `test_no_bulk_discount_below_threshold`, which confirms that 9 units still get no discount (974 cents).",
